  "finding": "The three alternate M1 groups have no connected tracks on MOSI, CLK or CSN0. SPI0_M0 belongs to expansion; SPI1_M0 overlaps Ethernet. The current SPI2_M0 group retains its routed SCLK and CSN0. GPIO N1/N2 provide DC/reset independently of the SPI interface. No pinmux change qualified.",
  "voltage_review": "All evaluated bank supply nets are nominally 3.3 V on the current CAD. The datasheet v2.1 recommended operating table places PMUIO1 and VCCIO4/5/6 on the 1.8-V line, whereas the reference diagram explicitly presents a 3.3-V PMUIO1 option and describes VCCIO4/5/6 as dual-voltage. The TRM also provides PMUIO1 1.8/3.3-V mode controls with hardware-source reset selection. Confirm supported silicon revision, regulator configuration, hardware status at reset and voltage-select programming before electrical qualification. VCCIO6 supply balls 1M4/1L5 lack attached local tracks in the checkpoint."
